{'answer': "The DeformView dataset offers pixel-level annotations of geometric inconsistencies in wide-baseline multi-view image sets. These annotations are created by applying controlled deformations to 3D object meshes and rendering them from multiple viewpoints. The deformations introduce known geometric inconsistencies, which are annotated at the pixel level to serve as ground truth for evaluating and training models like DEFECt3R.

These pixel-level annotations inform DEFECt3R's learning by providing explicit supervision during training. The classifier is trained to distinguish genuine geometric inconsistencies from visual deformations and reprojection artifacts. By using the annotations, DEFECt3R learns to reason about cross-view consistency directly from aligned feature pairs, enabling it to perform pixel-level localization with substantially fewer false positives than consistency-scoring approaches.

